/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20250509104645+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="b15d5b52-3d1a-4d06-8978-9c0d7584c924" date="D:20250509104854+10'00'" name="604265f8-b365-49f4-97b5-42d6ac29ffae" icon="Comment" page="9" rect="155.496000,297.950000,179.496000,321.950000" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q5b: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The sample size was powered to detect a moderate difference (d = 0.54) in muscle blood flow with and without compression with an a value of 0.05 and 80% statistical power. cohens d was referenced</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="9" rect="595.276000,229.950000,779.276000,321.950000"
/></text
